  "notes": "Introduced at Microsoft Build 2024 as the first multimodal model in the Phi-3 family; the Build post links a try-it page in Azure AI but lists only Phi-3-mini and Phi-3-medium under models as a service, so api access is not recorded. Not listed on the Retired Microsoft Foundry Models page. Version 3 of the Phi-3 technical report (arXiv 2404.14219v3) names OpenAI CLIP ViT-L/14 as the image encoder and phi-3-mini-128K-instruct as the decoder (cross-organisation component, not recorded as a relation). Microsoft reported benchmark results."
